Controller MessageManager integration tests
-------------------------------------------
ControllerMessageManagerIntegrationTest.sendMessagePersistsRealMessage - sent message is in the store
ControllerMessageManagerIntegrationTest.viewMessagesReturnsRealMessage - matching user reads the message
ControllerMessageManagerIntegrationTest.viewMessagesReturnsNoMessagesWhenNone - no message means No messages
ControllerMessageManagerIntegrationTest.viewMessagesReturnsNoMessagesForUnknownUser - unknown user sees nothing
ControllerMessageManagerIntegrationTest.sendMessageRejectsUnknownAgent - unknown agent sends nothing
ControllerMessageManagerIntegrationTest.sendMessageFindsSeededAgentByName - seeded agent found by name
ControllerMessageManagerIntegrationTest.viewMessagesJoinsMultipleMessages - two messages join with a newline
Notes: real MessageManager over a real SQLiteDataStore on a
test database behind the full Controller; users, access, and
audit stay mocked. The manager's user side stays mocked; it
is stored but never used by create or retrieve.
The Controller is constructed with a mocked
SessionManager as its 6th argument.
Run: .\gradlew test --tests "control.ControllerMessageManagerIntegrationTest" --console=plain
